<title>HONG KONG: Grand Hotel posts higher 1995/96 profit.</title>
<headline>Grand Hotel posts higher 1995/96 profit.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1996-09-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year ended June 30</p>
<p>(in million HK$ unless stated)</p>
<p>Earnings per A Shr (H.K. cents) 31.13 vs 22.43</p>
<p>Earnings per B Shr (H.K. cents) 3.11  vs 2.24</p>
<p>    Dividend A shr (H.K. cents)     13.5  vs 11.5</p>
<p>    Dividend B shr (H.K. cents)     1.35  vs 1.15</p>
<p>    Exceptional items		   nil   vs nil</p>
<p>    Net				     212.2 vs 152.9</p>
<p>    Turnover				485.4 vs 422.2</p>
<p>    Company name			  Grand Hotel Holdings Ltd</p>
<p>    Books close			   November 11-15</p>
<p>    Dividend payable		    November 29</p>
<p>NOTE - Grand Hotel is an investment holding and hotel business, Hang Lung Development Co Ltd owns 68.39 percent of its A shares and 62.52 percent of its B shares.</p>
<p>Total dividend for year is 20.5 H.K. cents (including interim dividend of seven cents) vs 18 cents per 'A' share and 2.05 cents (including interim dividend of 0.70 cents) vs 1.8 cents per 'B' share.</p>
<p>-- Hong Kong Newsroom (852) 2843 6368</p>
</text>
